<speak>
From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your daily briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">17022026</say-as>.
<break time="1s"/>
In politics.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Iran</emphasis> and the United States reached agreed "guiding principles" in indirect nuclear talks in Geneva, with Foreign Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔæbːɑːs ʔæɾæɢt͡ʃiː">Abbas Araghchi</phoneme> saying Tehran would return with detailed proposals within two weeks. A final deal is not imminent, as <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="xɑːmeˈneɪ">Khamenei</phoneme> maintained tough rhetoric and Iran continued live missile drills at the Strait of <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="hoɾˈmuːz">Hormuz</phoneme>.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Turkey</emphasis> received a landmark declaration from imprisoned Kurdish leader <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈœdʒalan">Abdullah Öcalan</phoneme>, who announced the end of a four-decade armed campaign by the Kurdistan Workers' Party that killed tens of thousands. He called the next phase "democratic integration," though Ankara has not yet formally responded.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Russia's</emphasis> lower house voted three hundred ninety-three to thirteen to give the Federal Security Service authority to shut down internet, mobile, phone, and postal services nationwide. The bill needs only upper chamber and presidential approval, representing a major wartime escalation in state censorship powers.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">The United States</emphasis> President Donald Trump said he would decide "pretty soon" on arms sales to Taiwan, despite a direct warning from Chinese President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɕi tɕin.pʰiŋ">Xi Jinping</phoneme> to handle the matter with prudence. The two leaders are scheduled to meet in Beijing in April, making any sale before then a sharp provocation.
<break time="900ms"/>
In conflict and security.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Lebanon's</emphasis> government set a four-month deadline to disarm <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ħizb‿ɑlˈlɑːh">Hezbollah</phoneme> north of the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="liˈtɑːni">Litani</phoneme> River, extending the ceasefire zone forty kilometres further north. Secretary-General <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nɑˈʕiːm ˈqɑːsɛm">Naim Qassem</phoneme> rejected the timeline as serving Israel's goals, leaving the ceasefire without an enforcement path.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Russia</emphasis> struck twelve Ukrainian regions with four hundred drones and thirty missiles overnight, killing three energy workers near <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="slɔˈvjɑnsk">Slovyansk</phoneme>, hours before a third round of United States-brokered Geneva peace talks began. Neither side has shifted its position, and the Kremlin warned against expecting progress.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Sudan's</emphasis> army drones killed at least twenty-eight people at a crowded market in North <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɔːɾdəˈfɑːn">Kordofan</phoneme>, while a separate strike hit a displacement shelter housing women and children in West <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="kɔːɾdəˈfɑːn">Kordofan</phoneme>. Both sides now bomb from above in a three-year war that has killed at least forty thousand people and displaced twelve million.
<break time="900ms"/>
On the economy.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">The United Kingdom's</emphasis> unemployment rate climbed to five point two percent in the final quarter of twenty twenty-five, the highest since twenty twenty-one, with youth joblessness reaching fourteen percent. Analysts estimate the pace of annual increase is the fastest in the Group of Seven.
<break time="900ms"/>
In science.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">China's</emphasis> Southeast University published a technique for growing two-dimensional molybdenum disulfide wafers one hundred times faster than existing methods, producing a six-inch single-crystal sheet that could succeed silicon. The material enables thinner, more efficient transistors as conventional chips approach their physical size limits.
<break time="1s"/>
That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.
</speak>